WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.260
Clinical observation watches and listens: what is the client doing?

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:07.840
Informal assessment sets up a non-standardized task: what

3
00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.940
can the client do on this task?

4
00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:13.620
Dynamic assessment teaches and examines the response: what changes

5
00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:16.780
with support, and can learning be used again?

6
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.280
You can observe communication during a standardized assessment.

7
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:24.920
The setting alone does not decide which method the observation represents.

8
00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:26.480
Begin with an independent attempt.

9
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:30.820
Teach using models, cues, feedback and practice.

10
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.720
Retest with reduced support or a new task.

11
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:37.220
The narrative example teaches character, setting, problem, action

12
00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:40.320
and outcome, then examines a new story.

13
00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:44.260
Repeating a language sample without instruction is not dynamic assessment.

14
00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:47.540
Keep the amount of help and the transfer evidence visible.

15
00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:51.180
Language sample analysis examines form, semantic intent,

16
00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:54.420
use, rate and sequencing across representative contexts.

17
00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:58.440
Semantic analysis looks at vocabulary variety, unusual

18
00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:01.800
substitutions, empty words and word finding.

19
00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:05.060
Establish story comprehension before interpreting retelling.

20
00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:07.860
Macrostructure is the story’s organization.

21
00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:12.460
Microstructure is grammar, vocabulary, syntax and cohesion.

22
00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:17.640
Higher-level language includes inference, motivation, causality and perspective.

23
00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:21.020
The class activities examine cause and effect, intention and play.

24
00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:24.740
Watch whether an action is repeated to obtain an outcome, how

25
00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:28.880
the child communicates a purpose, and whether symbolic play appears.

26
00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:32.940
Motor, sensory and access barriers can limit task performance.

27
00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:37.540
One unsuccessful toy interaction cannot establish absent understanding.

28
00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:40.820
Use the particular supplied checklist in its own context; do

29
00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:44.288
not merge its developmental ages with unrelated speech-sound norms.
